{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/262779-what-does-the-shining-example-gift-actually-do","id":262779,"title":"What does the Shining Example Gift actually do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-22T05:34:38-07:00","id":262779,"title":"What does the Shining Example Gift actually do?","content":"What does this ability do?<br /> &quot;For the rest of the scene, the werewolf can change a resisted or contested action (WoD Core p130) into an instant action.&quot; (Full text at bottom).<br /> It sounds something like a demon ability: Swift Resolution (Demon: The Descent -- Page 178), but more limited. (Obviously we are not talking about nwod-2e, but still perhaps these abilities have the same author or inspiration)<br /> Resisted actions are not defined in WoD core, but presumably it is an ability that is activated like &quot;Roll X+Y - target's Z&quot;, and also is non-instant, like either begin explicitly extended (&quot;each roll represents 5 minutes of X&quot;), or explicitly taking a long time: &quot;This ability may be activated after doing X for 5 minutes&quot;<br /> <b>To be clear: what is a Resisted Action, for purposed of this gift</b><br /> Contest actions are more well defined, and when there are extended (which they can be), then it more or less makes perfect sense.<br /> But there are still some questions:<br /> <b>Does it actually change the time required? Is it now done in 3 seconds?</b> So for example if done to a foot chase -- a extended contested. A single Dex+Athletics roll would me made, either the chased would be caught, or the chaser would give up, in 3 seconds?<br /> <b>Can a extended action be made contested by competing?</b> Rules on page 130 make it sound that way. Eg two people might have a race to carve a garden gnome out of wood. This is now a contested action so the ability can be used?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <b>[Honor 4 ] Shining Example ( Signs Of The Moon -- Page 103 )</b><br /><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Presence + Occult + Honor<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> An honorable werewolf can't rest on her laurels. Others have to see her being honest and impartial, putting them ahead of herself, and doing her duty to her pack and her totem. Sometimes, that's hard. Uncovering taint is never easy, but it's worse when she discovers her own alpha is a Bale Hound. Negotiating with a powerful spirit is an exhausting ordeal, but all most people will ever know is that tomorrow is much the same as today. Carrying the flame of truth is hard, especially when it's a truth most people would wish buried. Fortunately, just as the Elunim give Half Moons the ability to channel their honor backed with spiritual power, they empower particularly honorable behavior. A werewolf can use this Gift after performing a notable feat of honor.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Elunim turn their shadowed faces to the character. Whether they misunderstood her motives or see some flaw of which she is not yet aware, their displeasure is clear. The character loses a point of Essence. Failure: The character fails to impress the spirits.<br /> <b>Success</b> The werewolf's deeds impress the Elunim, showing that she is willing to put everything aside to do what is clearly right. For the rest of the scene, the werewolf can change a resisted or contested action (WoD Core p130) into an instant action. She can do this a number of times equal to her Honor Renown.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The character regains two points of Essence in addition to the effects of a success.<br /> <br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>(Cross posted from <a href=\"http://rpg.stackexchange.com/questions/48159/what-does-the-shining-example-gift-actually-do\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.stackexchange.com/questio...ft-actually-do</a>)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T06:38:16-07:00","id":262817,"title":"","content":"You can roll a gift, for example, without the target being able to contest it. Or flat out intimidate, or persuade, or attack someone without applying their defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T10:04:44-07:00","id":262930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>oxinabox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/262779-what-does-the-shining-example-gift-actually-do#post262779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>To be clear: what is a Resisted Action, for purposed of this gift</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I would say an action that reduces the dice-pool of the actor through the Resistance Attributes of the target, Defense, or Supernatural Tolerance. There isn't a single clear statement of this, but it is pretty solidly evident when you put all the pieces together as the intended meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Does it actually change the time required? Is it now done in 3 seconds?</b> </div> </div> </div>The power says nothing about turning extended actions into instant actions. The wording is clumsy, but I think there are only two coherent ways to handle this. Either it doesn't work on extended actions period - contested or resisted - or it only works on a single roll within an extended action to strip the other person in it of their ability to contest/resist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Can a extended action be made contested by competing?</b> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;made&quot; is the wrong word here. If two or more people are competing, the system models this as an extended contested action. Characters do not know their reality is being modeled this way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T10:12:21-07:00","id":262933,"title":"","content":"Attacking already is an instant action, so the Gift wouldn't allow you to ignore defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T11:15:27-07:00","id":262968,"title":"","content":"I'd let the Gift be used to ignore defense. The closest the 1st edition WoD core book comes to defining &quot;resisted actions&quot; is when it talks about using willpower to add to resistance, and Defense is one of the examples used. Compared to changing a contested action to instant, ignoring defense is a pretty weak option for something that requires a notable feat of Honor to activate, especially for the relatively low Defense values typical in 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T11:53:23-07:00","id":262985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/262779-what-does-the-shining-example-gift-actually-do?p=262933#post262933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attacking already is an instant action, so the Gift wouldn't allow you to ignore defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the nWOD 1e core doesn't really utilize the resistance attributes thing opting for contested for examples, there are plenty of examples of instant actions (generally supernatural powers) that are resisted. What's the logic is saying that you could combine this with Death 4 (instant action resisted with Stamina) and not an attack (instant action resisted with Defense)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T14:26:38-07:00","id":263129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/262779-what-does-the-shining-example-gift-actually-do?p=262933#post262933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attacking already is an instant action, so the Gift wouldn't allow you to ignore defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attacking is a resisted action, in which you generally subtract defense and/or armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T05:01:57-07:00","id":263626,"title":"","content":"It seems to me ignoring someone's Resistance Attributes / Defense / Supernatural Tolerance would be really, really, overpowered. Yes it costs a willpower and is renown 4, but you could use it to beat an opponent in pretty much anything you wish. That interpretation seems fishy to me.<br /> <br /> Also how notable is such a feat of honor? Can this ability be used after performing a feat that would constitute buying your first dot honor or does it have to be something great enough to constitute buying higher dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3931,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3931-vanbujm","user":"vanbujm","date":". 09-23-2014, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3931-vanbujm","name":"vanbujm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T07:35:48-07:00","id":263762,"title":"","content":"In the 1e rules, ignoring Resistance... really isn't that potent unless you're taking on something much more powerful than you. The ability to remove the targets ability to roll a Contested is way more powerful statistically speaking.<br /> <br /> Also... as honorable as your ST deems notable really. I wouldn't make it too high a bar simply because it will just come off as being a jerk and not letting the player use the power you let them buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T14:18:27-07:00","id":264115,"title":"","content":"Supernatural Tolerance generally only applies to contested rolls (rather than being a passive penalty to a resisted action). I can't think of an example off hand of a resisted action that a werewolf could perform that is penalized by more than one attribute/trait at a time. In practice, using the Gift on a resisted action is only worth 1-5 extra dice in most situations. There are some 1st edition dodge builds that it could be useful against (changeling wizened/skitterskulk fencers, etc.), but even in those situations the ability to pretty much guarantee succeeding at a contested action would probably be more useful/decisive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T15:24:36-07:00","id":264164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vanbujm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/262779-what-does-the-shining-example-gift-actually-do?p=263626#post263626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how notable is such a feat of honor? Can this ability be used after performing a feat that would constitute buying your first dot honor or does it have to be something great enough to constitute buying higher dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal interpretation of this generally boils to asking myself &quot;Is he putting himself, or his pack, or assets at risk because of one of his ethical viewpoints?&quot; If so, I'd allow the use of the gift. It's easy to issue judgement when there's no opposition. It's when there is opposition to the right judgement is when the Elunim lend their hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T18:43:37-07:00","id":264312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A werewolf can use this Gift <b>after </b>performing a notable feat of honor. </div> </div> </div>What does the <b>after</b> bit mean?<br /> Does that mean that you don't use this gift do do a honourable thing,<br /> you use it as a reward for doing the honourable thing.<br /> <br /> So first take the honourable action,<br /> and since you have been a good doggy,<br /> now you get to use this special power?<br /> <br /> Or is it a weird wording and it means that you can only ignore resisted/contested on roll where you are doing honor?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T20:42:14-07:00","id":264368,"title":"","content":"The phrasing does make sense most as the intent is that you have to do something honorable before activating this Gift. Though the sentence before it somewhat implies it should be used for honorable deeds as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T15:41:38-08:00","id":348595,"title":"","content":"What about the possibility of announcing previous honorable deed (IE the ones you used to raise honor) before invoking this gift...Kind of like Beowulf announcing his deeds as a way to cement his reputation. That actually makes a fair amount of sense to me. An elodoth standing up howling his deeds to the gathering before invoking this gift and making everyone shut their trap with dominance while he talks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T18:49:28-08:00","id":348684,"title":"","content":"I think the intention is that the Gift is used in the same scene that a notable act of honor occurred. After all, bringing up stuff the character did awhile back is &quot;resting on her laurels&quot;, but the power is vague enough that it can be run that way without contradicting anything if your group prefers that interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 12-24-2014, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}